openmediavault-immich (8.0.9) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add support for Immich external libraries. External libraries let
    Immich read photos/videos in place, without copying them into the
    upload library.
    - New "External libraries" page (Services -> Immich -> External
      libraries) to manage any number of mounts: shared folder,
      container path and a read-only option. Every entry is rendered
      into the Compose stack as
      '- ${{ sf:"<shared folder>" }}:<container path>[:ro]'.
    - New iterable data model conf.service.immich.library and the RPC
      methods getLibraries/getLibrary/setLibrary/deleteLibrary. The
      container path must be absolute, must not contain a colon, must
      not be "/" or "/data" and must be unique.
    - Changing an entry republishes the Compose stack; after Apply the
      containers are recreated with the new mounts. Shared folder
      changes are followed automatically through the Compose
      placeholder.
    - The settings page points to the new page. After applying, create
      the library in the Immich web interface (Administration ->
      External Libraries) using the configured container path.
    - The 8.0.9 migration adds the <libraries> node to existing
      configurations; fresh installations get it from create.d.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Require openmediavault-compose (>= 8.2.0): the stack lifecycle runs
    through the Compose plugin helper 'omv-compose-run', which was only
    added in Compose 8.2.0. On an older Compose plugin, applying the
    configuration failed with "omv-compose-run: not found" and the web
    UI showed a 500 error.
  * Fix the update detection: the latest upstream release is now read
    from the GitHub releases page redirect (github.com), not from the
    rate limited api.github.com endpoint, which failed once the
    anonymous API quota of the server IP was exhausted and left the
    "Latest version" field empty. The releases page redirect points at
    the newest release that is neither a draft nor a prerelease, so
    release candidates are skipped.
  * Show the stack file location in the Storage section (read only).
    The stack files are rendered by the Compose plugin into its shared
    folder and cannot be relocated here; the field documents the actual
    path again, next to the photo library and database folders.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 21:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.7) stable; urgency=medium

  * The Immich Docker Compose stack now follows the conventions of the
    openmediavault-compose plugin and is registered there, so it shows
    up in the Compose web UI (Services -> Compose -> Files / Services)
    and can be inspected, edited, started and stopped there as well.
    - The stack lives in the Compose plugin shared folder as
      <compose shared folder>/immich/immich.yml together with
      immich.env (plus the compose.yml/.env symlinks) - exactly the
      layout the Compose plugin uses for its own stacks.
    - On save the plugin publishes the stack through the Compose RPC
      (Compose.setFile); the Compose plugin renders the files, so this
      plugin no longer writes them itself (no double rendering).
    - The photo library and database shared folders are referenced
      through the Compose placeholder '${{ sf:"<name>" }}', so the
      Compose plugin resolves a changed shared folder path on deploy.
    - Lifecycle commands run through the Compose plugin helper
      omv-compose-run with the same --file/--env-file arguments as the
      Compose web UI.
    - The now unused 'composeDirRef' property (the stack files shared
      folder) is removed; the migration stops the previously rendered
      stack so its fixed container names are released. The photo
      library and the database are not touched.
    - The plugin now depends on openmediavault-compose; the Compose
      plugin shared folder must be configured before the settings can
      be saved.
    - Removing the plugin unregisters the stack from the Compose
      plugin (containers and generated stack files are removed, the
      photos/database shared folders are kept).

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 18:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.6) stable; urgency=medium

  * Extend the directory migration from the photo library to all three
    shared folders of the plugin (stack files, photo library, database).
    - "Test directories" validates every folder that was changed in the
      form (not saved yet) and lists the result per folder; folders that
      were not changed are not touched at all.
    - "Migrate data" copies every changed folder with rsync, verifies
      each copy against its source, records the migrations and starts
      the stack temporarily on the new locations so the result can be
      checked before saving. The migrated stack files folder becomes the
      working directory, the migrated photo and database locations are
      passed as environment variables.
    - Saving is refused per changed folder until its migration has been
      recorded. Afterwards only the data of the folders that were
      actually changed is removed.
    - The database folder is additionally validated for a PostgreSQL
      data directory (PG_VERSION marker) and for a matching PostgreSQL
      version.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Photo library migration: the settings page can now move the whole
    library to another shared folder without shell access.
    - New "Test directory" button validates the currently selected
      (not yet saved) photo library folder: it must exist, be
      writable, live on a local filesystem and either be empty or
      already carry the six .immich integrity markers - otherwise
      Immich would refuse to start. Free space is compared with the
      size of the current library.
    - New "Migrate library" button (with a confirmation dialog) stops
      the stack, copies the library with rsync (permissions, ACLs and
      xattrs preserved), verifies the copy against the source, records
      the migration and starts the stack temporarily on the new folder
      so the result can be checked in Immich. Nothing is saved yet.
    - Saving is refused while the photo library folder changes without
      a completed migration, and the data in the previous folder is
      removed (only the six Immich directories) by a background task
      that runs right after the settings have been saved.
    - rsync is added to the package dependencies.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 07 Oct 2026 10:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Packaging fix: the conf.service.immich_8.0.2.sh migration script
    was shipped without the executable bit, so upgrades from 8.0.2
    failed in postinst ("... is not executable") and left the package
    half-configured (fresh installs were not affected). The script is
    now committed with mode 755. Do not upgrade existing 8.0.2
    installations with the 8.0.3 deb, use this version instead.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 06 Oct 2026 18:50:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix the "Open Immich" button: the generated external URL was not
    URI-encoded, so the workbench externalRedirect/:url route (which
    matches a single path segment) never matched and the click ended
    on the 404 error page instead of opening the Immich web
    interface. The URL is now encoded with the encodeuricomponent
    filter, the same pattern used by the frpc and clouddrive2
    plugins.

 -- fffeng99999 <fffeng99999@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 06 Oct 2026 18:30:00 +0800

openmediavault-immich (8.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Storage configuration now uses shared folder references
    (sharedFolderSelect dropdowns) instead of plain path inputs: the
    stack files, the photo library and the PostgreSQL data each point
    to a shared folder on the data array. The ctl helper resolves the
    references with omv_get_sharedfolder_path, the Salt state with
    omv_conf.get_sharedfolder_path, and the engine module listens for
    shared folder changes to re-render on Apply.
  * Upgrade note for 8.0.1 installations: re-select the three shared
    folders on the settings page and apply the changes. Existing data
    is not moved automatically -- either create the shared folders at
    the previous locations or migrate the data before starting the
    stack again.
  * Pin the default image version to v3.2.4 (was the floating
    'release' tag) and report 'notinstalled' while the stack files are
    not rendered yet.

